course: dictionary
lesson: 11135
title: Widely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Widely is an adverb. It tells you how many people, how far, or how much something happens. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits: «English is the language most widely learned as a second language.» Here widely means by many people, so lots of people learn English as a second language.
explain: Widely can also mean over a large area: «mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world» means they moved over a huge area. It can mean a lot when things differ: «Prices vary widely» means some prices are very low and some are very high.
explain: Ask yourself: is it about many people, a big area, or a big difference? Then check by swapping in a simple phrase like "a lot" or "over a big area". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Widely means by many people or in many places, as in «widely known» and «widely used».
fact: Widely can mean over a large area or distance, as in «spread widely».
fact: Widely can mean a lot when things are far apart, as in «The answers varied widely».
fact: Mammoth bones are dug up in many countries because mammoths roamed widely across the northern half of the world.
fact: Other phrases to learn: «widely read», «widely spaced», «vary widely».
exercise: «English is the language most widely learned as a second language.» What does widely mean here? | Very quietly | Only by one person | *By many people, in many places
exercise: «Prices vary widely, from very cheap to very expensive.» What does widely mean here? | Slowly | Over one small area | *A lot, because the prices are far apart
exercise: «The sunflowers spread widely across the field.» What does spread widely mean? | Very quickly, in one spot | *Over a large area | Without any fuss
test: What does «widely known» mean? | Known very quietly | Known by only one person | *Known by many people
test: «This bird is widely found in Australia.» Does widely mean in many places, or only in one place? | *In many places | Only in one place | Very loudly
exam: «The answers varied widely, so the results were far apart.» What does varied widely mean? | *A lot, with big differences | Only by a few people | Slowly and softly
